    rdf:value """why we must not see each other any more now, and nothing he said changed those reasons, or could change them. So I left him after half an hour, and came up here to weep. Dear Bernhard comforted me very much, and he could not help saying it was an original situation for  him . But he was equal to it. The train time came and went, and Wilfrid was gone. He said I should never see him again.
Mr. Morgan came in as I was weeping, and I had to pretend it was a cold. 
Monday Nov. 15.97. Villa Rosa. Fiesole.
I was haunted by the fear – but the needless one – that Wilfrid would destroy himself: therefore a telegram telling me his address at Posillipo was """^^xsd:string ;
